Third-party code
================

Parts of this software are ported from ggml and llama.cpp
(https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors. The full notice is
LICENSES/ggml-MIT.txt, copied verbatim from llama.cpp's LICENSE at tag
b10353 (f8def7fe168bab245fbf15d3f18b26dbb1ef73c8). The ported parts:

- src/quants_iq_grids.h: the i-quant codebook grids and sign tables,
  verbatim from ggml/src/ggml-common.h (b10353).
- src/quants.c: the GGUF block layouts, the i-quant dequantizers
  (dequantize_row_iq*, ggml-quants.c b10353) and the UE4M3 scale conversion
  (ggml_ue4m3_to_fp32).
- src/quantize.c: the reference quantizers Q8_0, Q4_0, Q3_K, Q4_K and Q6_K,
  with ggml's make_qx_quants and make_qkx2_quants; the importance-weighted
  Q3_K and Q4_0 quantizers (quantize_row_q3_K_impl, quantize_row_q4_0_impl);
  and the MXFP4 writer (quantize_row_mxfp4_ref). Built without floating-point
  contraction, as Runner builds them, the reference writers' output is
  byte-identical to ggml b10353's built the same way
  (tests/fixtures/quant-golden). ggml's own Q4_K and Q6_K bytes change when
  its build fuses multiply-adds, so a llama.cpp build that does differs from
  both in about 1% of those super-blocks, by one rounding step.
- src/model.h: the xIELU activation, transcribed from ggml's op_xielu.
- src/kernels.metal: the Gated DeltaNet recurrence's lane layout in
  k_dn_recur (one simdgroup per value row of the state, the row's key
  columns across the lanes, simd_sum for both dot products), ported from
  ggml/src/ggml-metal/kernels/gated_delta_net.metal (kernel_gated_delta_net)
  at llama.cpp commit 0ec4027 (2026-10-30), newer than b10353 and under the
  same MIT License.

Several architectures are implemented to match llama.cpp's graph for them
(gpt-oss, afmoe, muse-glimmer, gemma4's per-layer embeddings, swiglu_oai);
the comments at those places name the llama.cpp source they were checked
against. Those are independent C implementations of the same arithmetic,
not copies of llama.cpp code.

src/ed25519.c (TweetNaCl, public domain) and src/mldsa/ (pq-crystals
dilithium, public domain / CC0, also Apache 2.0) are described in README.md,
"License".
